AB  - In the present study, we have done a comparative study on the efficacy of some currently used repurposed drugs: Oseltamivir (O), Favipiravir (F) and Hydroxychloroquine (H) in individual and in their combinational mode against CoV-2 infections. The ADME analysis has helped us to identify the inhibitory possibility of the tested drugs towards receptor 3CL<sup>pro</sup> protein of SARS-CoV-2. Various thermodynamical parameters obtained from Molecular Docking, Molecular dynamics (MD) and MMPBSA simulations like binding affinity, potential energy (E<sub>pot</sub>), RMSD, RMSF, SASA energy, interaction energies, Gibbs free energy (ΔG<sub>bind</sub>) etc. also helped us to verify the effectivity of mentioned drugs against CoV-2 protease.
