AB  - COVID19 convalescent plasma (CCP) has proven an effective treatment for outpatients, and CCP collected from vaccinated donors is among the few effective therapeutic options for immunocompromised patients. Despite this, most countries are still relying over in-hospital compassionate usages outside clinical trials. Given the need for early treatment, home transfusions are expecially needed. We review here the state of the art for out-of-hospital CCP transfusions and discuss solutions to potential burocratic hurdles.
