AB  - <p>Molnupiravir and Paxlovid are the only antivirals approved for COVID-19 treatment. Previous studies have evaluated their efficacy, tolerability, and viral clearance, but little is known about SARS-CoV-2 evolution under their pressure. Here the dynamics of genomic evolution of SARS-CoV-2 in 8 Molnupiravir-treated, 7 Paxlovid-treated and 5 drug-na&iuml;ve individuals at 4 time-points (Day 0, Day 2, Day 5 of treatment and Day 7) were in-depth investigated. SARS-CoV-2 strains under Molnupiravir pressure were characterized by a higher genetic diversity compared to Paxlovid and no-drug pressure (mean&thinsp;&plusmn;&thinsp;SE: 18.66x10<sup>&minus;&thinsp;4</sup>&plusmn;2.06x10<sup>&minus;&thinsp;4</sup> vs. 3.34x10<sup>&minus;&thinsp;4</sup>&plusmn;0.84x10<sup>&minus;&thinsp;4</sup> vs. 3.10x10<sup>&minus;&thinsp;4</sup>&plusmn;0.84x10<sup>&minus;&thinsp;4</sup>, P&thinsp;=&thinsp;0.0003), with a peak between Day 2 and Day 5. Molnupiravir drove the emergence of more G-A and C-T transitions than other mutations (P&thinsp;=&thinsp;0.031), regardless of SARS-CoV-2 genes. SARS-CoV-2 under Molnupiravir pressure did not show selective evolution different than that under Paxlovid or no-drug pressure, with the only exception of orf8 (dN&thinsp;&gt;&thinsp;dS, P&thinsp;=&thinsp;0.001); few amino acid mutations were enriched consistently at specific sites. No evidence of RdRp or Mpro mutations conferring resistance to Molnupiravir or Paxlovid was found.</p> <p>This proof-of-concept study defines the SARS-CoV-2 within-host evolution during antiviral treatment, confirming the higher in vivo variability induced by Molnupiravir respect to Paxlovid and controls, albeit not resulting in selection of resistance mutations.</p>
