AB  - <p>REGEN-COV, a combination of the monoclonal antibodies casirivimab and imdevimab, has been approved as a treatment for high-risk patients infected with SARS-CoV-2 within 5 days of their diagnosis. We used the data repositories of Israel&rsquo;s largest healthcare organization to determine the real-world effectiveness of REGEN-COV treatment against COVID-19 related hospitalization, severe disease, and death. We compared patients infected with the delta variant of SARS-CoV-2 and treated with REGEN-COV (n&thinsp;=&thinsp;289) to those infected but untreated with REGEN-COV (n&thinsp;=&thinsp;1,294). Patients were matched and further adjusted on demographic and clinical characteristics, with estimated treatment effectiveness defined as one minus the hazard ratio. Treatment effectiveness of REGEN-COV was 55.2% (95% CI: 21.5&ndash;74.5%) in preventing COVID-19 hospitalization, 59.4% (95% CI: 20.2&ndash;79.4%) in preventing severe COVID-19, and 93.8% (95% CI: 54.4&ndash;99.2%) in preventing COVID-19 death in the 28 days after treatment. In conclusion, REGEN-COV was effective in reducing the risk of severe sequelae in high-risk COVID-19 patients.</p>
